// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FoodClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2953099861" "NTU Nutrient Packs"
// DetailString :
"P353941285" "These packs contain everything a human body needs in 3 ounces of powder. Usually mixed into water to make a thin broth, NTU Nutrient Packs are emergency rations that were first developed during the Hamidon Wars to ensure that soldiers and refugees had enough to survive. Now-a-days they come in many varieties and flavors, but are still considered a last resort for most people."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P994161475" "The Turning Point"
// DetailString :
"P3189948057" "When Dr. Helix's treatment of genetic damage in the Ghouls returned much of their mental faculties to them, the Resistance had found itself with a great many helping hands, but more hungry bellies than it could fill. Calvin Scott called upon you to aid in the surface raids to ensure that the Resistance had enough supplies to go around."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DurayClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2597913344" "Colonel Duray"
// DetailString :
"P4193147972" "Colonel Duray captured Helix and Crow, but he failed in capturing you as well. How did he survive your last encounter?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1784770266" "When Dr. Helix's treatment of genetic damage in the Ghouls returned much of their mental faculties to them, the Resistance had found itself with a great many helping hands, but more hungry bellies than it could fill. Calvin Scott called upon you to aid in the surface raids to ensure that the Resistance had enough supplies to go around.<br><br>With the supply line stable, Scott sent you, Helix, and Crow on a covert mission to cripple the PPD T.E.S.T. supply facility in Lambda Sector. During the operation, however, Crow and Helix were capture by Colonel Duray and his men. Though you defeated Duray, your friends had already been carried off."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - RescueHelixClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1944555001" "Helix"
// DetailString :
"P4044515178" "You rescued Helix and she informed you that Colonel Duray wasn't the one who captured her, it was Crow!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P4151040277" "When Dr. Helix's treatment of genetic damage in the Ghouls returned much of their mental faculties to them, the Resistance had found itself with a great many helping hands, but more hungry bellies than it could fill. Calvin Scott called upon you to aid in the surface raids to ensure that the Resistance had enough supplies to go around.<br><br>With the supply line stable, Scott sent you, Helix, and Crow on a covert mission to cripple the PPD T.E.S.T. supply facility in Lambda Sector. During the operation, however, Crow and Helix were capture by Colonel Duray and his men. Though you defeated Duray, your friends had already been carried off.<br><br>Calvin Scott was worried that the sensitive strategic information that Crow and Helix had would soon be used by the Loyalists against the Resistance. He sent you with Tunnel Rat and Splice to break into Lambda Sector and free Helix and Crow. You and Tunnel Rat found Helix, but learned that Crow hadn't been captured, he was a traitor!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission4Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P132988854" "When Dr. Helix's treatment of genetic damage in the Ghouls returned much of their mental faculties to them, the Resistance had found itself with a great many helping hands, but more hungry bellies than it could fill. Calvin Scott called upon you to aid in the surface raids to ensure that the Resistance had enough supplies to go around.<br><br>With the supply line stable, Scott sent you, Helix, and Crow on a covert mission to cripple the PPD T.E.S.T. supply facility in Lambda Sector. During the operation, however, Crow and Helix were capture by Colonel Duray and his men. Though you defeated Duray, your friends had already been carried off.<br><br>Calvin Scott was worried that the sensitive strategic information that Crow and Helix had would soon be used by the Loyalists against the Resistance. He sent you with Tunnel Rat and Splice to break into Lambda Sector and free Helix and Crow. You and Tunnel Rat found Helix, but learned that Crow hadn't been captured, he was a traitor!<br><br>With the knowledge of Crow's treachery, Calvin Scott prepared the Resistance defenses. He sent you to tunnel Junction 221 to meet the oncoming Loyalist forces at a bottleneck. The battle was fierce, but the timely attack on the main body by the most untrained Ghouls ended up turning the tide."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ResistanceSupportersClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P210107862" "Resistance Supporters"
// DetailString :
"P2108871271" "Crow told you that the Resistance supporters in the senate have been singled out to his superiors. Soon they will be arrested."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ResistanceCellsClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2719976596" "Resistance Cells"
// DetailString :
"P2405152907" "Crow also told you that the various Resistance cells that he was made aware of during his time with the Resistance have also had their locations revealed to his superiors."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MrHClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1627015122" "Mr. H"
// DetailString :
"P1368024230" "When you found Crow he was on his cell phone talking to a man named Mr. H. You searched the phone for recent calls but it appears that number is blocked."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - TheTurningPointSouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P906742173" "Crow's Cell Phone"
// tDetailString :
"P3725346280" "You kept Crow's cell phone, wondering if one day it will ring, but it never has. It is a constant reminder to you of his betrayal of the Resistance during:<br><br><color deepskyblue>The Turning Point</color><br><br>It all began when Dr. Helix's treatment of genetic damage in the Ghouls returned much of their mental faculties to them. The Resistance had found itself with a great many helping hands, but more hungry bellies than it could fill. Calvin Scott called upon you to aid in the surface raids to ensure that the Resistance had enough supplies to go around.<br><br>With the supply line stable, Scott sent you, Helix, and Crow on a covert mission to cripple the PPD T.E.S.T. supply facility in Lambda Sector. During the operation, however, Crow and Helix were capture by Colonel Duray and his men. Though you defeated Duray, your friends had already been carried off.<br><br>Calvin Scott was worried that the sensitive strategic information that Crow and Helix had would soon be used by the Loyalists against the Resistance. He sent you with Tunnel Rat and Splice to break into Lambda Sector and free Helix and Crow. You and Tunnel Rat found Helix, but learned that Crow hadn't been captured, he was a traitor!<br><br>With the knowledge of Crow's treachery, Calvin Scott prepared the Resistance defenses. He sent you to tunnel Junction 221 to meet the oncoming Loyalist forces at a bottleneck. The battle was fierce, but the timely attack on the main body by the most untrained Ghouls ended up turning the tide.<br><br>Calvin Scott prepared to evacuate the Resistance hideout but had one last task for you. Working with a familiar Arachnos Blood Widow, Dahlia, the two of you were sent to find and assassinate Crow for his treachery. You tracked him to Doctor Demetrios Vasilikos' old genetics laboratory. There you found Crow talking to someone named Mr. H and informing him that the data was sent. You followed your orders, killing Crow, but to this day you are unsure just who Mr. H is or what convinced Crow that this was the time to betray, that this was the turning point."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3917732311" "We're holding the Ghouls in reserve. Hrm, we really need a better name for them. They've earned that. The grunts are calling them <color yellow>Cupcakes</color>, I don't pretend to know why, but it's stuck.<br><br>The real issue right now is food. We've doubled our numbers but our logistics are completely incapaable of keeping up. We don't want to tip our hand and let Tyrant's forces know we've gotten reinforcements, but we need food badly.<br><br>Luckily we've gotten the stigma that anything we do has nothing to do with our actual plans. I sent a team to hit a storehouse jam packed with foodstuffs bound for <color yellow>New Vegas</color>. The plan was to hit the place, take everything, then burn it down, but something went wrong and we've lost communication with the team. "
// AcceptString :
"P437308099" "Assist the Storehouse Raid"
// SendOffString :
"P135103014" "Top priority is to get that team out of there. Our bellies can ache a little longer, but if we start abandoning comrades, then moral is going to plummet."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3956575307" "We need that food badly."
// TaskTitle :
"P1908576382" "<color deepskyblue>The Turning Point</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2803742992" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: Belly Aching</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2188232309" "The distinct smell of smoke is in the air long before you arrive, so you aren't surprised to see the warehouse interior is up in flames."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2991554950" "You rescued the hit team and secured enough food to hold hunger at bay, for awhile."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1756968488" "Small fragment groups of The Syndicate remain opposed to Mr. Yin's alliance with us. Normally this isn't an issue, but with the given circumstances every setback, no matter how minor, could end up snowballing this situation out of control.<br><br>You did well, {HeroName}. The other teams we sent out had similar luck and now TPN is reporting that Resistance terrorists are attacking indiscriminently across Neutropolis and Imperial City setting fires in an apparent 'last desperate hurrah'.<br><br>One day, when this war is over, people are going to see that we did the only thing we could do to win, and that was, unfortunately, to attack the weakest link in Cole's super powered regime... the people who aren't super at all."
// RandomFameString :
"P856364347" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3550458066" "According to TPN, our <i>campaign of terror</i> is still underway. Our next order of business is to completely prove them right. This is our <i>last desperate hurrah!</i> At least, it will certainly seem like it.<br><br>We're going to throw everything we've got into the fray. Everything <i>they know</i> that we've got.<br><br>Once they think we're commited the PPD, T.E.S.T. and Powers Division is going to do everything they can to contain our forces. Once they do they'll look to strike directly at me and the other leaders. And that's where we'll trap them.<br><br>But before that happens, I want you, Crow, and Helix doing black ops."
// AcceptString :
"P2539281824" "Covert Ops"
// SendOffString :
"P587157542" "Hit the main T.E.S.T. facility. We need to switch up our tactics just a bit to keep Cole's forces on their toes and make them think we're trying to confuse them."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2238960761" "Destroy Main T.E.S.T. facility."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P428096751" "Get in, plant your bombs, and get out."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P687516283" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: Hit 'Em Where It Hurts</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1448409765" "Helix deactivates the alarm, and nobody appears to notice you and Crow entering the facility."

